; CoCoSID: a three-voice, SID-style music player for the TRS-80 Color
; Computer. All sound is made in software: three wavetable oscillators
; are summed and written to the 6-bit DAC at $FF20. Interrupts stay off;
; all timing comes from instruction cycle counts.
;
; Timing (0.895 MHz CPU):
;   sample      77 cycles, so about 11.6 kHz
;   mixer pass  227 samples, about 20 ms; one envelope frame
;   tick        one sequencer step plus three mixer passes, about 60 ms
;
; Song data:
;   song list   one per voice, one pattern number per byte. 0 stops the
;               voice, $FF restarts the whole song.
;   pattern     a stream of commands; see CMDTABLE.
;   instrument  15 frames of 4 bytes, built in RAM at INSTRS by command 2:
;                 +0  pointer to the middle of a 256-byte wave table
;                 +2  pitch offset in notes, times 2
;                 +3  unused
;               Frames 0-2 are the attack, 3-11 the sustain (looped while
;               the note is held), 12-14 the release. Volume envelopes
;               come from switching to half or quarter amplitude waves.

          SETDP  $48

V_NOTE    EQU    0                        ; note number times 2 [ssynth_freq]
V_INSTR   EQU    1                        ; instrument now sounding (2 bytes) [ssynth_wavetable]
V_IBASE   EQU    3                        ; instrument selected by the pattern (2 bytes) [ssynth_note_wave]
V_FRAME   EQU    5                        ; envelope frame, times 4 [ssynth_wave_frag]
V_PATPTR  EQU    6                        ; next pattern command, 0 = fetch a pattern (2 bytes) [ssynth_voice_ptr]
V_SONGPTR EQU    8                        ; next song list entry (2 bytes) [ssynth_song_ptr]
V_DUR     EQU    10                       ; ticks left before the note releases [ssynth_note_duration]
V_GAP     EQU    11                       ; ticks of rest left [ssynth_pause_duration]
V_GAPLEN  EQU    12                       ; rest after the last note, 0 = tied to the next [ssynth_slur_note]
V_BEND    EQU    13                       ; pitch bend added to the frequency, voice 1 only (2 bytes) [ssynth_pitch_alteration]
V_BRATE   EQU    15                       ; added to V_BEND every mixer pass (2 bytes) [ssynth_pitch_glide]
V_SIZE    EQU    18                       ; size of a voice record [sizeof_ssynth]

PIA0CRA   EQU    $FF01
PIA0CRB   EQU    $FF03
PIA1DA    EQU    $FF20
PIA1CRA   EQU    $FF21
PIA1CRB   EQU    $FF23
DSKREG    EQU    $FF40

VOICE1    EQU    $4815                    ; voice records, V_SIZE bytes each (RAM) [synth1]
